# spec_id: eravos.organism.breath · version 1.0.0 · phase P8.4 · status canonical
# source: v10 VAGAL_INSTRUMENT (polyvagal breath instrument, VAGAL mode)
identity:
  id: eravos.breath ; label: Breath ; icon: ◎ ; accent: "#8844ff"
  comp_intent: A paced-breathing guide that is also an instrument — the music swells on the inhale and falls on the exhale, so you can breathe with it together.
  novelty: Only organism whose clock is a breath cycle (seconds per phase) rather than bars; emits a continuous breath control signal.
engine:
  patterns (v10): COHERENCE 5-0-5-0 · 4-7-8 · BOX 4-4-4-4 · EXTENDED 4-0-8-0 · ENERGIZE 2-0-2-0 · HANGING TREE 6-2-6-2 ; custom [in, hold, out, hold] 0..12 s
  signal: ConstantSource → port 'breath' (mod, 0..1) shaped per phase: inhale ease-in rise, holds flat, exhale ease-out fall — wire to organ breath, filter cutoff, reverb mix
  voice: built-in pad (3 detuned tri + LP) whose pitch follows a drawn phase curve (v10 "inhale rises · exhale falls"), in song key ; optional off (control-only)
  tempo link: optional — cycle length snapped to whole bars at current BPM
  sessions: count cycles, elapsed ; gentle bell (sine 2 partials) on phase change, optional
config: pattern enum def COHERENCE ; custom[4] ; voiceOn bool ; curve points ; bell bool ; tempoLink bool ; level
hooks: breath.hook.breath_out (out ; modulation ; port breath) ; phase_out (out ; event_bus ; breath:phase {phase, cycle, time}) ; STD.audio_out ; STD.theory_in
ui: hero = breath orb (grows/shrinks with the real signal value), phase label (INHALE/HOLD/EXHALE), countdown arc ; pattern select with v10 descriptions ; curve editor
safety note in UI: "Stop if you feel dizzy." (4-7-8 and ENERGIZE) — plain text, no medical claims
tests: BOX → phases each 4.0 s ± 10 ms ; breath port = 1 at end of inhale, 0 at end of exhale ; tempoLink → cycle scaled to the nearest whole number of bars (≥ 1) at the current BPM (amended P14: 10 s at 60 BPM is 2.5 bars, so it becomes 8 s)

